## 1.1 Theorem on Compounding Error Boundaries in Recurrent Handoffs
Let $\mathcal{A} = \{A_1, A_2, \dots, A_T\}$ represent an ordered sequence of generative agents. Let $v_0$ be the ideal latent constraint embedding. Let $\delta_t \in [0, 1]$ be the local semantic drift parameter introduced at sequence depth $t$.
Theorem 1. If local drift accumulation is strictly bounded such that $\delta_t \leq \epsilon < 1$ for all steps $t$, the global Semantic Trust Index $\mathcal{ST_I}(T)$ scales inversely as a geometric decay curve governed by sequence depth, yielding a worst-case convergence limit profile:
$$\mathcal{ST_I}(T) \geq \exp\left(-\gamma \cdot \frac{T+1}{2} \cdot \epsilon\right)$$ 
## 1.2 Mathematical Derivation & Proof
By construction, the cumulative trust equation weights late-stage agent deviations linearly using the coefficient $w_t = \frac{t}{T}$. We can expand the internal sum parameter within our primary exponential function as follows:
$$\sum_{t=1}^{T} w_t \cdot \delta_t = \sum_{t=1}^{T} \left(\frac{t}{T}\right) \delta_t$$ 
Substituting our absolute local ceiling constraint $\epsilon$ for every occurrence of $\delta_t$, we extract the constant scalars outside the processing array boundaries:
$$\sum_{t=1}^{T} \left(\frac{t}{T}\right) \delta_t \leq \frac{\epsilon}{T} \sum_{t=1}^{T} t$$ 
Applying Gauss’s formula for arithmetic series progressions ($\sum_{t=1}^{T} t = \frac{T(T+1)}{2}$), the step-depth variable $T$ in the denominator cancels out neatly:
$$\frac{\epsilon}{T} \left[ \frac{T(T+1)}{2} \right] = \epsilon \cdot \frac{T+1}{2}$$ 
Because the outer transformation function $f(x) = \exp(-x)$ decreases monotonically over its entire domain, substituting this maximized upper ceiling sum back into our exponent yields the formal minimum bounds configuration for the global pipeline:
$$\mathcal{ST_I}(T) = \exp\left(-\gamma \sum_{t=1}^{T} w_t \delta_t\right) \geq \exp\left(-\gamma \cdot \frac{T+1}{2} \cdot \epsilon\right) \quad \blacksquare$$ 
